<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Poesía náhuatl II and III (Ángel María Garibay Kintana)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965, 1968</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Spanish edition and translation of much of the manuscript</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Cantares mexicanos (ed. Miguel León-Portilla, UNAM)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2011</span><span class="sg-chain-h">first complete Spanish translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Cantares Mexicanos: Songs of the Aztecs (John Bierhorst)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1985</span><span class="sg-chain-h">complete transcription and English translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Flower, Song, Dance: Aztec and Mayan Poetry (David Bowles)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translations of selected poems</span></li></ul></section>
